.TH "ODIR-LABEL" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-label \- label: Label a tape
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
label [storage=<storage>] [sd=<sd>] [volume=<volume>] [pool=<pool>] [slot=<slot>[,...]] [catalog=<catalog>] [slots=<slots>] [drive=<drive>] [barcodes] [barcode] [encrypt] [yes] [device=<device>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Writes a Bareos label onto a new medium (file or tape) through the Storage Daemon and creates the matching Media record in the catalog. Only a labelled volume can be used for backups. The command changes both the medium and the catalog. Missing values are asked for: storage, volume name, slot and pool.
.PP
Volume names may contain letters, digits and :.\-_/ but must not start with /. slot= greater than 0 also sets the InChanger flag; on an autochanger without slot= the Director asks for the slot. drive= selects the drive and defaults to 0. encrypt creates a new key for hardware (LTO) encryption and stores it in the catalog.
.PP
barcodes labels every volume of an autochanger with the name read from its barcode; slots= restricts this to a slot list such as 1\-5,8, and yes answers the confirmation question. Only autochanger storages qualify.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "label"
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "sd=<sd>"
Storage name (as storage=) (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "volume=<volume>"
Volume name (text)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.TP
.B "slot=<slot>[,...]"
Slot (text; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.TP
.B "slots=<slots>"
Slots (list or ranges) (text)
.TP
.B "drive=<drive>"
Drive number (number)
.TP
.B "barcodes"
Use the barcodes as names (keyword)
.TP
.B "barcode"
Use the barcodes as names (keyword)
.TP
.B "encrypt"
Encrypt (keyword)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.TP
.B "device=<device>"
Device name (text)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "label storage=File volume=Full\-0001 pool=Full"
label one file volume into pool Full
.TP
.B "label barcodes storage=Autochanger pool=Scratch slots=1\-5 yes"
label slots 1 to 5 with their barcodes, without asking
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
